## Flow built and validated ✓

**File:** `VendorInvoiceProcessing/VendorInvoiceFlow/VendorInvoiceFlow.flow`

### What was built

| Node | Type | Role |
|---|---|---|
| **New Invoice in SharePoint** | `uipath.connector.trigger.…file-created` | Fires when any file lands in SharePoint |
| **Download Invoice PDF** | `uipath.connector.…download-file` | Downloads the PDF so IxP can process it |
| **Extract Invoice Fields** | `uipath.ixp.invoiceixp-cef0d447-ixp` | Runs the **InvoiceIXP** model — pulls invoice number, vendor, date, amount, line items |
| **Build SAP Payload** | `core.action.script` | Reads the extracted fields and assembles a clean JSON object |
| **Post Invoice to SAP** | `core.action.http.v2` (manual POST) | HTTP POST to SAP — URL is a placeholder |
| **Done** | `core.control.end` | Ends the flow |

**Edge chain:** trigger → download → extract → build payload → post to SAP → done

**Validation:** passes (`flow validate` exit 0). The one warning is expected — it flags that the SAP node label mentions "SAP" but uses raw HTTP, which is correct since IT hasn't provided a live SAP connector. The node is wired to POST `https://sap-placeholder.example.com/api/invoices`; swapping in the real URL is all that's needed.

**Format:** run and clean (6 nodes repositioned, 3 resized).

